/**
 * @file browse.html
 * @brief Root shell document for the CloudAvid File Portal single-page application (SPA).
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @section overview 📖 Overview
 *
 * @subsection eli5_overview 🧒 ELI5 Summary
 *
 * Imagine you have a really nice picture frame that never changes. The frame
 * has a pretty top piece (the navigation bar with the logo), a pretty bottom
 * piece (the footer with the company name), and a big empty space in the
 * middle. Every time you want to show a different picture, you just swap the
 * picture in the middle — you never throw away the frame! This file IS that
 * frame. It's the one-and-only HTML page that your browser ever loads. All
 * the "pages" you see (Home, Browse, etc.) are really just different pictures
 * being slotted into the middle of this frame by JavaScript.
 *
 * @subsection core_responsibilities Core Responsibilities
 *
 * - **SPA Shell:** Serves as the single, persistent HTML document; the browser
 *   never performs a full-page navigation away from this file.
 * - **Asset Pipeline Bootstrap:** Loads every external resource the application
 *   needs — fonts, design-token CSS, component CSS, page-specific CSS, and the
 *   favicon — in the correct dependency order.
 * - **Persistent Chrome:** Renders the navigation bar (`<nav>`) and footer
 *   (`<footer>`) once; they survive all client-side route transitions.
 * - **Content Mount Point:** Provides `<main id="app">` as the sole DOM node
 *   the client-side router targets for injecting/swapping page content.
 * - **Script Orchestration:** Loads five JavaScript modules (`i18n`, `banner`,
 *   `home`, `browse`, `router`) in dependency order at the bottom of `<body>`
 *   so the DOM is fully parsed before any script executes.
 * - **Internationalization (i18n) Hooks:** Sprinkles `data-i18n` attributes on
 *   translatable text nodes so the i18n module can find and replace them at
 *   runtime.
 * - **Progressive Enhancement of Language Toggle:** Embeds an inline SVG globe
 *   icon inside `#langBtn` so the language-switch button is immediately styled
 *   without waiting for an icon font or sprite sheet.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @section architecture 🏗️ Architectural Flow (DOT Diagram)
 *
 * The diagram below visualises how the browser processes this file from the
 * initial HTTP response through to an interactive, routed SPA.
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph architecture {
 *   rankdir=TB;
 *   node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, color="#9CA3AF"];
 *   edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, color="#6B7280"];
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_head {
 *     label="<head> — Render-Blocking Resources";
 *     style="dashed"; color="#9CA3AF"; fontname="Helvetica"; fontsize=11;
 *
 *     meta        [label="Meta Tags\n(charset, viewport)", fillcolor="#DBEAFE"];
 *     title       [label="<title>\nCloudAvid • File Portal", fillcolor="#DBEAFE"];
 *     preconnect  [label="Preconnect\nfonts.googleapis.com\nfonts.gstatic.com", fillcolor="#E0E7FF"];
 *     gfonts      [label="Google Fonts\nManrope · Cinzel\nVazirmatn · Sora", fillcolor="#E0E7FF"];
 *     tokens_css  [label="tokens.css\nDesign Tokens", fillcolor="#FEF3C7"];
 *     base_css    [label="base.css\nReset & Defaults", fillcolor="#FEF3C7"];
 *     comp_css    [label="components.css\nReusable UI Parts", fillcolor="#FEF3C7"];
 *     home_css    [label="home.css\nHome Page Styles", fillcolor="#FEF3C7"];
 *     browse_css  [label="browse.css\nBrowse Page Styles", fillcolor="#FEF3C7"];
 *     favicon     [label="Favicon\nfiles-logo.webp", fillcolor="#DBEAFE"];
 *   }
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_body {
 *     label="<body> — Visible DOM";
 *     style="dashed"; color="#9CA3AF"; fontname="Helvetica"; fontsize=11;
 *
 *     page_div [label="div.page\n(Layout Wrapper)", fillcolor="#D1FAE5"];
 *     nav      [label="nav.nav\n(Persistent Navbar)", fillcolor="#CFFAFE"];
 *     app      [label="main#app\n(Route Viewport)", fillcolor="#FCE7F3"];
 *     footer   [label="footer.footer\n(Persistent Footer)", fillcolor="#CFFAFE"];
 *   }
 *
 *   subgraph cluster_scripts {
 *     label="<body> — Scripts (Parse-Order)";
 *     style="dashed"; color="#9CA3AF"; fontname="Helvetica"; fontsize=11;
 *
 *     i18n_js   [label="i18n.js\nTranslation Engine", fillcolor="#EDE9FE"];
 *     banner_js [label="banner.js\nHero Banner Logic", fillcolor="#EDE9FE"];
 *     home_js   [label="home.js\nHome Page Builder", fillcolor="#EDE9FE"];
 *     browse_js [label="browse.js\nBrowse Page Builder", fillcolor="#EDE9FE"];
 *     router_js [label="router.js\nClient-Side Router", fillcolor="#FEE2E2"];
 *   }
 *
 *   meta -> title -> preconnect -> gfonts -> tokens_css -> base_css -> comp_css -> home_css -> browse_css -> favicon [style=invis];
 *
 *   page_div -> nav;
 *   page_div -> app;
 *   page_div -> footer;
 *
 *   i18n_js -> banner_js -> home_js -> browse_js -> router_js [label="load order"];
 *
 *   router_js -> app [label="innerHTML swap", style=dashed, color="#EF4444"];
 *   i18n_js -> nav [label="translate data-i18n", style=dashed, color="#7C3AED"];
 *   i18n_js -> footer [label="translate data-i18n", style=dashed, color="#7C3AED"];
 *   home_js -> app [label="render()", style=dashed, color="#2563EB"];
 *   browse_js -> app [label="render()", style=dashed, color="#2563EB"];
 *   banner_js -> app [label="inject banner", style=dashed, color="#2563EB"];
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @section sequence 🔄 Execution Sequence (PlantUML Diagram)
 *
 * This sequence diagram shows the runtime lifecycle from the moment the
 * browser requests `index.html` to the first interactive paint.
 *
 * @startuml
 * skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
 * skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
 * skinparam participantPadding 20
 * skinparam boxPadding 10
 *
 * actor User
 * participant Browser
 * participant "index.html" as HTML
 * participant "Google Fonts" as GF
 * participant "tokens.css\nbase.css\ncomponents.css\nhome.css\nbrowse.css" as CSS
 * participant "i18n.js" as I18N
 * participant "banner.js" as Banner
 * participant "home.js" as Home
 * participant "browse.js" as Browse
 * participant "router.js" as Router
 * participant "main#app" as App
 *
 * User -> Browser : Navigate to /
 * Browser -> HTML : GET /index.html
 * activate HTML
 *
 * HTML -> GF : <link preconnect> + font CSS
 * activate GF
 * GF --> Browser : WOFF2 font files
 * deactivate GF
 *
 * HTML -> CSS : <link rel="stylesheet"> × 5
 * activate CSS
 * CSS --> Browser : Parsed CSSOM
 * deactivate CSS
 *
 * HTML --> Browser : DOM fully parsed
 * deactivate HTML
 *
 * Browser -> I18N : Execute i18n.js
 * activate I18N
 * I18N -> I18N : Detect locale, build dictionary
 * I18N -> Browser : Translate all [data-i18n] nodes
 * deactivate I18N
 *
 * Browser -> Banner : Execute banner.js
 * activate Banner
 * Banner -> Banner : Register banner renderer
 * deactivate Banner
 *
 * Browser -> Home : Execute home.js
 * activate Home
 * Home -> Home : Register home renderer
 * deactivate Home
 *
 * Browser -> Browse : Execute browse.js
 * activate Browse
 * Browse -> Browse : Register browse renderer
 * deactivate Browse
 *
 * Browser -> Router : Execute router.js
 * activate Router
 * Router -> Router : Read window.location.pathname
 * Router -> App : innerHTML = matchedRoute.render()
 * activate App
 * App --> Browser : First Contentful Paint
 * deactivate App
 *
 * Router -> Router : Listen popstate & click[data-link]
 * deactivate Router
 *
 * User -> Browser : Click <a data-link>
 * Browser -> Router : Intercept click, pushState
 * Router -> App : innerHTML = newRoute.render()
 * @enduml
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @section deepdive 🧩 Block-by-Block Deep Dive
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_doctype Block 1 — DOCTYPE Declaration
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Forces the browser into **standards mode** so every CSS box-model
 * calculation, layout algorithm, and rendering behaviour follows the W3C
 * specification rather than legacy "quirks mode" heuristics.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * It's like telling the referee "we're playing by the official rules" before
 * the game starts, so nobody argues about what's fair.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * `<!doctype html>` is the shortest valid doctype for HTML5+. It carries no
 * version number or DTD URI because HTML is now a "living standard." Without
 * it, Internet Explorer and some older engines fall back to quirks mode where
 * `width` includes padding+border (IE5 box model), percentage heights resolve
 * differently, and `<table>` font inheritance breaks.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None — this is a parser directive, not a DOM element.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Browser rendering mode set to "no-quirks."
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <!doctype html>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_html Block 2 — `<html>` Root Element
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Establishes the document's **language** (`en`) and **text direction**
 * (`ltr`), informing screen readers, search engines, and CSS logical
 * properties how to interpret and render content.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the big box that holds everything. The labels on the box say
 * "English" and "read left-to-right" so everyone knows which way to read.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * - `lang="en"` enables correct hyphenation (`hyphens: auto`), tells
 *   assistive technologies which speech-synthesis profile to load, and helps
 *   Google determine the page's primary language.
 * - `dir="ltr"` sets the base directionality for the Unicode Bidirectional
 *   Algorithm (UBA). When the i18n module switches to Farsi, it can flip this
 *   to `dir="rtl"`, which cascades to every descendant via CSS logical
 *   properties (`margin-inline-start`, etc.).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Root element available to all scripts as
 * `document.documentElement`.
 *
 * **🔗 Dependencies:** The `i18n.js` module reads and mutates both `lang` and
 * `dir` at runtime.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <html lang="en" dir="ltr">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_head Block 3 — `<head>` Element (Container)
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Houses all **metadata, style, and resource-hint** declarations that the
 * browser must process before it can begin layout and paint.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * Think of `<head>` as the instruction manual you read BEFORE you start
 * building your LEGO set. It doesn't show you the LEGO pieces (that's
 * `<body>`), but it tells you what tools and stickers you'll need.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Everything inside `<head>` is non-visual. The browser constructs a
 * parallel CSSOM (CSS Object Model) from the stylesheets listed here.
 * Rendering is blocked until all render-critical CSS is downloaded and parsed.
 * The `<head>` is parsed sequentially, which is why resource hints
 * (`preconnect`) precede the actual font `<link>`.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None (opening tag).
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Fully configured CSSOM, document title, favicon, and
 * preconnected sockets.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <head>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_meta_charset Block 4 — Meta Charset Declaration
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Declares the character encoding as **UTF-8**, ensuring every glyph — from
 * English letters to Farsi script (وزیرمتن) to emoji (☁️) — decodes
 * correctly.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This tells the browser which alphabet book to use. UTF-8 is the alphabet
 * book that knows ALL the languages in the world, plus smiley faces!
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * The HTML spec requires this meta tag to appear within the first 1024 bytes
 * of the document. If absent or declared late, the browser performs encoding
 * sniffing, which can cause a re-parse of the entire document and potential
 * XSS vulnerabilities via charset mismatch attacks (e.g., UTF-7 injection).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `document.characterSet === "UTF-8"`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <meta charset="utf-8" />
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_meta_viewport Block 5 — Meta Viewport Configuration
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Instructs mobile browsers to set the layout viewport width to the device's
 * screen width and the initial zoom level to 100%, enabling **responsive
 * design**.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * Without this, your phone would try to show the entire website shrunk down
 * to a tiny size like looking at a poster through binoculars held backwards.
 * This tag says "show it at normal size, please!"
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * - `width=device-width` maps the CSS `px` unit to the device-independent
 *   pixel (DIP) grid, making media queries like `@media (max-width: 768px)`
 *   fire at the expected breakpoints.
 * - `initial-scale=1` prevents iOS Safari from zooming out on landscape
 *   rotation. Note: `maximum-scale=1` and `user-scalable=no` are
 *   intentionally omitted to preserve accessibility (pinch-to-zoom).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `window.innerWidth` matches CSS media query widths.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_title Block 6 — Document Title
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Sets the text displayed in the browser tab, bookmark list, and search
 * engine results page (SERP) snippet.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the name tag stuck on the browser tab so you can find this page
 * when you have a million tabs open (we've all been there 😉).
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Format follows the `Brand • Section` pattern for SEO breadcrumb clarity.
 * The bullet (`•`, U+2022) is a common separator that survives all encodings
 * and renders cleanly at small tab-title font sizes. The router may update
 * `document.title` on each route change for accessibility (screen readers
 * announce title changes).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `document.title === "CloudAvid • File Portal"`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <title>CloudAvid • File Portal</title>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_preconnect_google Block 7 — Preconnect to Google Fonts API
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Opens an early TCP+TLS connection to `fonts.googleapis.com` so that when
 * the browser encounters the font stylesheet `<link>`, the handshake is
 * already complete, shaving **100–300 ms** off font load time.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * Imagine you're ordering pizza. This step is like calling the pizza place
 * ahead of time and saying "get the oven hot!" — so when you actually order,
 * the pizza comes faster.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * `rel="preconnect"` performs DNS resolution, TCP handshake, and TLS
 * negotiation. This is a non-blocking resource hint; if the connection
 * isn't used within ~10 seconds, the browser may close it. This link targets
 * the API server that returns the `@font-face` CSS, NOT the server that hosts
 * the actual font binary files (that's `fonts.gstatic.com`, handled next).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None (resource hint).
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** A warm socket to `fonts.googleapis.com`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_preconnect_gstatic Block 8 — Preconnect to Google Fonts Static CDN
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Opens an early TCP+TLS connection to `fonts.gstatic.com` — the CDN that
 * serves the actual WOFF2/TTF binary font files. The `crossorigin` attribute
 * is mandatory here because font files are fetched with CORS.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * The first call went to the pizza restaurant's phone line (Google API). This
 * second call goes to the delivery driver's garage (Google Static) so he can
 * start his car early.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Without `crossorigin`, the browser opens a non-credentialed connection, but
 * fonts are always fetched as anonymous CORS requests. This mismatch means
 * the preconnected socket can't be reused, and the browser opens a second
 * connection anyway — wasting the preconnect entirely. The `crossorigin`
 * attribute (equivalent to `crossorigin="anonymous"`) ensures the connection's
 * credential mode matches the font fetch.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None (resource hint).
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** A warm, CORS-compatible socket to `fonts.gstatic.com`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_google_fonts Block 9 — Google Fonts Stylesheet
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Fetches a dynamically generated CSS file from Google that contains
 * `@font-face` declarations for four font families at the specified weight
 * ranges, giving the application its distinctive typographic identity.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is like going to the sticker store and picking out four different
 * fancy letter styles: one for titles, one for normal reading, one for Farsi
 * text, and one for special headings.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * | Font Family | Weight Range | Purpose |
 * |-------------|-------------|---------|
 * | **Manrope** | 400–800 | Primary sans-serif for body copy. Variable font, so a single file covers Regular through ExtraBold. |
 * | **Cinzel** | 400–700 | Decorative serif for brand/hero headings. |
 * | **Vazirmatn** | 300–700 | Persian/Arabic script support for RTL i18n. |
 * | **Sora** | 400, 500, 600 | Secondary geometric sans-serif, likely used for UI controls. |
 *
 * `display=swap` sets `font-display: swap` in every generated `@font-face`,
 * meaning text is painted immediately with a fallback font and re-rendered
 * once the web font arrives (FOUT rather than FOIT). This is optimal for Core
 * Web Vitals (Largest Contentful Paint).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Preconnected sockets from Blocks 7 & 8.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Four font families available in the CSSOM; text renders
 * with `font-family: 'Manrope', …` etc.
 *
 * **🔗 Dependencies:** Consumed by `tokens.css` (custom properties like
 * `--font-body`), which is loaded next.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400..800&family=Cinzel:wght@400..700&family=Vazirmatn:wght@300..700&family=Sora:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_tokens_css Block 10 — Design Tokens Stylesheet
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `tokens.css`, a file containing CSS custom properties (variables) that
 * define the design system's primitive values: colours, spacing scale, font
 * stacks, border radii, shadows, and breakpoints.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the box of crayons. Before you draw anything, you pick which
 * colours you'll use. `tokens.css` is where all the colour names live, like
 * `--color-primary` (the blue crayon) and `--space-4` (four steps wide).
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * By loading tokens first, every subsequent stylesheet can reference
 * `var(--token-name)` without worrying about cascade order. This follows the
 * **Design Token → Base → Components → Pages** layering convention used by
 * systems like Salesforce Lightning and IBM Carbon.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Font families from Google Fonts (Block 9) — tokens likely
 * map `--font-body: 'Manrope', sans-serif`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Custom properties on `:root` available to all downstream
 * CSS.
 *
 * **🔗 Dependencies:** Consumed by `base.css`, `components.css`, `home.css`,
 * `browse.css`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/tokens.css">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_base_css Block 11 — Base Stylesheet
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `base.css`, which contains a CSS reset (e.g., `*, *::before,
 * *::after { box-sizing: border-box }`) and default element styles
 * (typography, link colours, body background).
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * Every browser has its own weird default look — some make bullet points big,
 * some make headings a different size. `base.css` is like saying "everyone
 * start from the same starting line" so the race is fair.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Loaded after `tokens.css` so that reset rules can reference custom
 * properties (e.g., `body { font-family: var(--font-body); }`). This layer
 * should contain ZERO class selectors — only element, pseudo-element, and
 * attribute selectors.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Custom properties from `tokens.css`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Normalised default styles for all HTML elements.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/base.css">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_components_css Block 12 — Components Stylesheet
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `components.css`, containing reusable, page-agnostic UI component
 * classes such as `.btn`, `.btn-sm`, `.btn-icon`, `.nav`, `.nav-bar`,
 * `.nav-logo`, `.nav-actions`, `.footer`, and `.page`.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * These are the LEGO instruction booklets for little builds — a button, a
 * menu bar, a footer. You can use the same little build on any page, just
 * like you can put the same LEGO car on any LEGO table.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Components are styled with BEM-ish flat classes (`.nav-logo-text`,
 * `.nav-actions`) rather than deeply nested selectors for specificity
 * control and tree-shaking friendliness. This file must load before any
 * page-specific CSS so that page overrides win by source order without
 * needing `!important`.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Custom properties from `tokens.css`, reset from `base.css`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Styled `.btn`, `.nav`, `.footer`, `.page` components.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/components.css">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_home_css Block 13 — Home Page Stylesheet
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `home.css`, containing styles exclusive to the home/landing route
 * (hero banner, feature cards, call-to-action sections, etc.).
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * The Home page is the "welcome mat" of the website. This stylesheet picks
 * the welcome mat's colour, pattern, and size.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Although this is an SPA and not every route uses these styles, loading them
 * upfront in `<head>` avoids a Flash of Unstyled Content (FOUC) if the user
 * navigates to `/` and the styles haven't been fetched yet. For applications
 * with many page-specific stylesheets, code-splitting via dynamic
 * `<link>` injection would be preferable; for two pages (home + browse),
 * upfront loading is the simpler, faster strategy.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Tokens, base, components.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Styles for home-page-specific DOM injected by `home.js`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/home.css">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_browse_css Block 14 — Browse Page Stylesheet
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `browse.css`, containing styles exclusive to the file-browsing route
 * (directory listings, file cards, breadcrumbs, grid/list toggle, etc.).
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * The Browse page is like a library shelf view. This stylesheet decides how
 * the books (files) are arranged — in a grid or a list — and what their
 * spines look like.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Same rationale as `home.css` above — loaded eagerly to prevent FOUC. The
 * file likely uses CSS Grid or Flexbox for the directory listing layout and
 * may include `:empty` or `:has()` states for empty-directory placeholders.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Tokens, base, components.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Styles for browse-page-specific DOM injected by
 * `browse.js`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/browse.css">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_favicon Block 15 — Favicon
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Declares the page's favicon using a WebP image, displayed in the browser
 * tab, bookmarks bar, and mobile home-screen shortcut.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the tiny picture next to the page's name in the tab bar. It's like
 * the little logo sticker on the spine of a book so you recognise it on the
 * shelf.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * WebP is chosen over PNG for its superior compression (typically 25–35%
 * smaller). Modern browsers universally support WebP favicons. The
 * `rel="icon"` without a `type` attribute lets the browser sniff the MIME
 * type from the HTTP response (`image/webp`). For legacy IE support (if
 * needed), a `/favicon.ico` at the web root would be a fallback.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Tab icon rendered.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon/files-logo.webp">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_head_close Block 16 — `</head>` Closing Tag
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Signals the end of the document metadata section. The browser has now
 * collected all information needed to construct the CSSOM and can begin
 * processing the `<body>`.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * We've finished reading the instruction manual. Time to open the LEGO box!
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * At this point the parser transitions from the "in head" insertion mode to
 * "after head" and then "in body." The CSSOM from all five stylesheets plus
 * Google Fonts has been (or is being) constructed. The render tree won't
 * be built until both the DOM and CSSOM are ready.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** All `<head>` children.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Parser state transition.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * </head>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_body Block 17 — `<body>` Opening Tag
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Opens the document body — the container for all **visible** content.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is where we start placing the LEGO bricks on the baseplate. Everything
 * from here on is stuff people can actually see and click on.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * The `<body>` element has no explicit `class` or `id`. Global page layout is
 * delegated to the nested `<div class="page">` wrapper, keeping `<body>`
 * styling minimal (typically just `margin: 0` from the reset in `base.css`).
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** CSSOM from `<head>`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `document.body` reference available to scripts.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <body>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_page_div Block 18 — Page Layout Wrapper
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Wraps the entire visible page in a single `<div>` with class `.page`,
 * providing a CSS layout context (likely `display: flex; flex-direction:
 * column; min-height: 100vh`) that pushes the footer to the bottom even
 * when content is short (sticky footer pattern).
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the picture frame that holds the top bar, the middle content, and
 * the bottom bar together in a nice vertical sandwich.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Using a `.page` wrapper rather than styling `<body>` directly provides:
 * 1. A clean specificity boundary (class vs element selector).
 * 2. A stacking context for potential z-index layering (modals, toasts).
 * 3. The ability to add a max-width container or side padding without
 *    affecting body-level backgrounds or fixed-position elements.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** None.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Flex column container for nav, main, footer.
 *
 * **🔗 Dependencies:** Styled by `components.css` (`.page` class).
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <div class="page">
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_nav Block 19 — Navigation Bar
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Renders the persistent top navigation containing the logo, brand name,
 * subtitle, external website link, and language toggle button. This element
 * is **never destroyed** by the SPA router.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the roof of our house — it's always there, no matter which room
 * (page) you're standing in. It has the family name sign (logo), a doorbell
 * to the main website, and a magic button that changes the language.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * - `<nav class="nav">` — Semantic landmark element; assistive tech exposes
 *   it as a navigation role. The `.nav` class hooks into `components.css`
 *   for visual styling (backdrop blur, sticky positioning, z-index).
 * - `<div class="nav-bar">` — Inner flex container that horizontally
 *   distributes logo (start) and actions (end) with `justify-content:
 *   space-between`.
 * - `<a class="nav-logo" href="/" data-link>` — The logo anchor navigates to
 *   the home route. `data-link` is a **critical SPA attribute**: the router
 *   intercepts clicks on any `[data-link]` anchor, calls
 *   `history.pushState()`, and re-renders `#app` instead of letting the
 *   browser perform a full page load.
 * - `<img src="/assets/icon/logo.png" alt="CloudAvid">` — Company logo image.
 *   The `alt` text ensures screen readers announce the brand name.
 * - `<div class="nav-logo-text">` — Stacks brand name and subtitle
 *   vertically beside the logo image.
 * - `<strong data-i18n="brand">CloudAvid</strong>` — The `data-i18n="brand"`
 *   attribute marks this node for translation by `i18n.js`. The text
 *   "CloudAvid" is the English fallback visible before the i18n module runs.
 * - `<span data-i18n="subtitle">File Portal</span>` — Same i18n mechanism
 *   for the subtitle.
 * - `<div class="nav-actions">` — Groups the right-side controls.
 * - `<a class="btn btn-sm" href="https://cloudavid.com" data-i18n="website">
 *   Website</a>` — External link to the main website. `btn btn-sm` applies
 *   button-like styling at a small size. The text "Website" is translatable.
 *   Note: no `data-link` attribute, so this performs a normal navigation away
 *   from the SPA.
 * - `<button id="langBtn">` — Language toggle. `btn-icon` styles it as a
 *   square icon button. The `title` provides a tooltip and accessible name.
 *   Clicking it triggers the `i18n.js` module to cycle the locale (e.g.,
 *   `en` ↔ `fa`), flip `dir`, and re-translate all `[data-i18n]` nodes.
 * - The inline SVG is a globe icon from the Feather Icons set. Using inline
 *   SVG (rather than an `<img>` or icon font) allows the icon to inherit
 *   `currentColor` for theming and eliminates an extra HTTP request.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** `components.css` for styling; `i18n.js` for translation;
 * `router.js` for `data-link` interception.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Rendered nav bar with clickable logo, external link, and
 * language toggle.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <!-- NAV — always visible, never destroyed -->
 * <nav class="nav">
 *     <div class="nav-bar">
 *         <a class="nav-logo" href="/" data-link>
 *             <img src="/assets/icon/logo.png" alt="CloudAvid">
 *             <div class="nav-logo-text">
 *                 <strong data-i18n="brand">CloudAvid</strong>
 *                 <span data-i18n="subtitle">File Portal</span>
 *             </div>
 *         </a>
 *         <div class="nav-actions">
 *             <a class="btn btn-sm" href="https://cloudavid.com" data-i18n="website">Website</a>
 *             <button class="btn btn-sm btn-icon" id="langBtn" type="button" title="Toggle language">
 *                 <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
 *                     stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
 *                     <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
 *                     <line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12" />
 *                     <path
 *                         d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z" />
 *                 </svg>
 *             </button>
 *         </div>
 *     </div>
 * </nav>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_main Block 20 — Main Content Mount Point
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * This empty `<main>` element is the **sole injection target** for the
 * client-side router. Every route handler renders its HTML string into
 * `document.getElementById('app').innerHTML`.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the blank canvas in the middle of the picture frame. The robot
 * painter (JavaScript router) keeps drawing new pictures on it every time
 * you click a link, but the frame never moves.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * - `<main>` is a semantic landmark that assistive tech exposes as the
 *   document's primary content region. There should be only one `<main>` per
 *   document (spec recommendation).
 * - `id="app"` is the contract between `index.html` and `router.js`. The
 *   router performs `document.getElementById('app')` to locate this node.
 * - The element starts **empty** in the HTML source. Content appears only
 *   after `router.js` executes and matches the current URL to a route
 *   handler (e.g., `home.js`'s `render()` or `browse.js`'s `render()`).
 * - Because the router replaces `innerHTML`, any event listeners attached
 *   to children of `#app` must either be re-attached after each render or
 *   use event delegation on `#app` itself.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Rendered HTML from `home.js`, `browse.js`, or `banner.js`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Visible page content between nav and footer.
 *
 * **🔗 Dependencies:** `router.js` (write), `home.js` (content), `browse.js`
 * (content), `banner.js` (content).
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <!-- MAIN CONTENT — this is the only part that changes -->
 * <main id="app"></main>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_footer Block 21 — Footer
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Renders the persistent page footer with a copyright notice and a link to
 * the company's main website. Like the nav, it is **never destroyed** by
 * route changes.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the bottom mat of the house — it always stays. It says "Made by
 * CloudAvid" and has a link to visit them.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * - `<footer class="footer">` — Semantic `contentinfo` landmark. The
 *   `.footer` class maps to `components.css` for styling (padding, border-top,
 *   flex row with `justify-content: space-between`).
 * - `<span>© 2025 CloudAvid Co</span>` — Static copyright. Not marked
 *   `data-i18n`, so it appears unchanged in all locales. The year `2025`
 *   could be generated dynamically by JS if desired.
 * - `<a href="https://cloudavid.com">cloudavid.com</a>` — External link.
 *   No `data-link` because it navigates away from the SPA.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** `components.css` for styling.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Rendered footer at bottom of viewport.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <!-- FOOTER — always visible, never destroyed -->
 * <footer class="footer">
 *     <span>© 2025 CloudAvid Co</span>
 *     <a href="https://cloudavid.com">cloudavid.com</a>
 * </footer>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_page_close Block 22 — Closing `</div>` for `.page`
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Closes the `.page` layout wrapper opened in Block 18.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * We put the last side on the sandwich box. Snap!
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * This terminates the flex column container. All three children (`nav`,
 * `main#app`, `footer`) are now laid out. The `main` element typically gets
 * `flex: 1` in `components.css` so it absorbs remaining vertical space,
 * pushing the footer to the bottom.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** All children (nav, main, footer).
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Completed flex layout.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * </div>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_script_i18n Block 23 — Script: Internationalization Engine
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `i18n.js`, the translation module that detects the user's locale,
 * manages a dictionary of key→translation mappings, and replaces the
 * `textContent` of every element bearing a `data-i18n` attribute.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the translator friend who speaks both English and Farsi. When you
 * press the globe button, they re-read every sign in the house and flip it
 * to the other language.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Loaded first among all scripts because other modules (`banner.js`,
 * `home.js`, `browse.js`) may call i18n utility functions (e.g.,
 * `t('key')`) when rendering their templates. The module likely:
 * 1. Reads `localStorage` or `navigator.language` for initial locale.
 * 2. Sets `document.documentElement.lang` and `.dir`.
 * 3. Exposes a global function or object (e.g., `window.i18n` or
 *    `window.t()`).
 * 4. Attaches a click handler to `#langBtn` to toggle locales.
 * 5. Walks the DOM to apply translations to all `[data-i18n]` elements.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** DOM elements with `data-i18n` attributes; `#langBtn`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Translated UI; `lang`/`dir` set on `<html>`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <script src="/assets/js/i18n.js"></script>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_script_banner Block 24 — Script: Banner Module
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `banner.js`, which likely exports or registers a function to
 * render a hero banner component into `#app` on the home route.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the artist who paints the big "Welcome!" poster at the top of the
 * home page.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Loaded after `i18n.js` so it can use the `t()` function for translatable
 * banner copy. It may export a `renderBanner()` function consumed by
 * `home.js`, or it may register itself in a shared route-component registry.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** `i18n.js` for translations; `home.css` for styling.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Banner HTML string or DOM fragment.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <script src="/assets/js/banner.js"></script>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_script_home Block 25 — Script: Home Page Module
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `home.js`, which defines the rendering logic for the home/landing
 * route (`/`). It likely exports a `render()` function that returns an HTML
 * string to be injected into `#app`.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the instruction booklet for building the "Welcome Home" room
 * inside our picture frame.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * The module probably:
 * 1. Imports/uses `banner.js`'s output as a sub-component.
 * 2. Builds an HTML template with translatable strings via `t()`.
 * 3. Registers itself with the router (e.g., `router.register('/',
 *    homeRender)`), or the router imports its `render` function directly.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** `i18n.js`, `banner.js`, `home.css`.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `render()` function for the `/` route.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <script src="/assets/js/home.js"></script>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_script_browse Block 26 — Script: Browse Page Module
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `browse.js`, which defines the rendering logic for the file-browsing
 * route (e.g., `/browse` or `/browse/:path`). It likely fetches directory
 * listings from an API and renders them as a file grid or list.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the instruction booklet for building the "Library Shelves" room
 * where you can see all the files and folders.
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * The module probably:
 * 1. Exports a `render(path)` async function that fetches a JSON directory
 *    listing from an API endpoint.
 * 2. Constructs a DOM fragment with breadcrumbs, folder cards, and file
 *    cards.
 * 3. Attaches click handlers (or uses event delegation on `#app`) for
 *    folder navigation via `data-link` anchors.
 * 4. Supports query parameters for sort order, view mode (grid/list), etc.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** `i18n.js`, `browse.css`, API data.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `render()` function for the `/browse` route.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <script src="/assets/js/browse.js"></script>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_script_router Block 27 — Script: Client-Side Router
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Loads `router.js`, the **last** script, which initialises the client-side
 * routing system. It reads the current URL, matches it to a registered
 * route handler, and renders the corresponding page into `#app`.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * This is the traffic cop. When you click a link, instead of leaving the
 * house and coming back, the traffic cop just tells the painter to change the
 * picture in the middle of the frame. Much faster!
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * Loaded last because it depends on all page modules (`home.js`, `browse.js`)
 * being already registered/available. The module likely:
 * 1. Defines a route table mapping URL patterns to render functions:
 *    `{ '/': homeRender, '/browse': browseRender, '/browse/:path': browseRender }`.
 * 2. Calls the initial render based on `window.location.pathname`.
 * 3. Attaches a **delegated click handler** on `document` (or `document.body`)
 *    that intercepts clicks on any `<a>` with `data-link`:
 *    - `event.preventDefault()` — stops the browser from navigating.
 *    - `history.pushState({}, '', href)` — updates the URL bar.
 *    - Calls the matched route's `render()` and sets `#app.innerHTML`.
 * 4. Listens for the `popstate` event (browser back/forward buttons) and
 *    re-renders accordingly.
 * 5. May update `document.title` after each navigation for accessibility.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** All page modules, `#app` DOM node, `data-link` anchors.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** Live SPA navigation; content rendered in `#app`.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * <script src="/assets/js/router.js"></script>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @subsection block_body_close Block 28 — Closing `</body>` and `</html>`
 *
 * **🎯 Purpose:**
 * Closes the document body and the root HTML element, signalling the end of
 * the document to the parser.
 *
 * **🧒 ELI5:**
 * We've finished building everything. Time to close the LEGO box lid and
 * admire our creation!
 *
 * **⚙️ Technical Details:**
 * When the HTML parser reaches `</html>`, it fires the `DOMContentLoaded`
 * event (if not already fired). Since all `<script>` tags are
 * non-`defer`/non-`async` and placed at the bottom of `<body>`, they execute
 * synchronously before the parser reaches these closing tags. Therefore,
 * `DOMContentLoaded` fires after all five scripts have executed, and the
 * initial route has already been rendered into `#app`.
 *
 * **📥 Inputs:** Fully parsed and scripted document.
 *
 * **📤 Outputs:** `DOMContentLoaded` and eventually `load` events.
 *
 * **💻 Actual Code:**
 *
 * ```html
 * </body>
 *
 * </html>
 * ```
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * @section conventions 📐 Conventions Table
 *
 * The following table catalogues every custom attribute, ID, and CSS class
 * used in `index.html`, along with the consuming module(s).
 *
 * | Attribute / Selector          | Type           | Consumed By          | Purpose                                                                 |
 * |-------------------------------|----------------|----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
 * | `data-link`                   | HTML attribute | `router.js`          | Marks `<a>` tags for SPA client-side navigation (prevent default).       |
 * | `data-i18n="brand"`           | HTML attribute | `i18n.js`            | Translation key for the brand name ("CloudAvid").                        |
 * | `data-i18n="subtitle"`        | HTML attribute | `i18n.js`            | Translation key for the subtitle ("File Portal").                        |
 * | `data-i18n="website"`         | HTML attribute | `i18n.js`            | Translation key for the website link text ("Website").                   |
 * | `id="app"`                    | HTML ID        | `router.js`          | The sole DOM mount point for route-rendered content.                     |
 * | `id="langBtn"`                | HTML ID        | `i18n.js`            | Language toggle button; i18n module attaches a click listener.           |
 * | `.page`                       | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Full-height flex column wrapper (sticky footer pattern).                 |
 * | `.nav`                        | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Top navigation landmark styling.                                        |
 * | `.nav-bar`                    | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Inner horizontal flex container for nav content.                         |
 * | `.nav-logo`                   | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Logo anchor styling (flex row, gap, alignment).                          |
 * | `.nav-logo-text`              | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Vertical stack for brand name + subtitle text.                           |
 * | `.nav-actions`                | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Right-aligned group for nav action buttons/links.                        |
 * | `.btn`                        | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Base button styling (padding, border-radius, cursor).                    |
 * | `.btn-sm`                     | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Small-size modifier for buttons (reduced padding/font-size).             |
 * | `.btn-icon`                   | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Square icon-only button modifier (equal width/height, centred content).  |
 * | `.footer`                     | CSS class      | `components.css`     | Footer landmark styling (border-top, padding, flex row).                 |
 * | `lang` (on `<html>`)          | HTML attribute | `i18n.js`, Browser   | Current document language; mutated by i18n on locale switch.             |
 * | `dir` (on `<html>`)           | HTML attribute | `i18n.js`, CSS       | Text directionality (`ltr`/`rtl`); mutated by i18n on locale switch.     |
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
